SUMMARY:REFUGE: Film Screening and Panel at the City of Raleigh Museum
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a screening of the 2023 documentary REFUGE. The film follows a former white nationalist who confronts his beliefs after connecting with a Muslim Refugee community in Georgia. \nA panel following the screening will discuss how people and communities work through division. Heavy snacks will be provided. \nPanelists Include: Ashley Glimasinski\, Maryam S. Khan\, Esq\, Rev. Timothy McMahan King\, and Dr. Omer Abdalla Omer.
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/refuge-film-screening-and-panel-at-the-city-of-raleigh-museum/
LOCATION:City of Raleigh Museum\, 220 Fayetteville Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
